From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:34:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] mt76x02: read the packet numbers after the MAC has stopped

A watchdog restart reads the packet number each hardware key reached
(MT_WCID_IV) into the key, and mac80211 installs the keys again from
there. mt76x02_reset_state() read them first thing, with the MAC still
enabled: the frames the hardware went on to send before
MT_MAC_SYS_CTRL was cleared used numbers past the ones read, and after
the restart the key started from the old value and used them again.
With CCMP that is the same nonce on two different frames, pairwise or
group key alike.

Read them after the MAC and the DMA have been stopped. Keys with a
software packet number are not affected: the number is taken when the
frame is built and the frames still queued are dropped.

Found by reading the source in a security review of the Wi-Fi drivers;
no watchdog restart was provoked to see it on the air.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/mt76x02_mmio.c
+++ b/mt76x02_mmio.c
@@ -528,12 +528,22 @@ static void mt76x02_reset_state(struct m
 
 	clear_bit(MT76_STATE_RUNNING, &dev->mphy.state);
 
+	dev->mt76.vif_mask = 0;
+	dev->mt76.beacon_mask = 0;
+}
+
+/* Take the packet numbers the hardware reached, for the keys to be installed
+ * again with them after the restart. Only once the MAC has stopped sending:
+ * a frame that goes out after they are read uses a number the key then
+ * starts from again, and the same number protects two different frames.
+ */
+static void mt76x02_sync_tx_pn(struct mt76x02_dev *dev)
+{
+	lockdep_assert_held(&dev->mt76.mutex);
+
 	rcu_read_lock();
 	ieee80211_iter_keys_rcu(dev->mt76.hw, NULL, mt76x02_key_sync, NULL);
 	rcu_read_unlock();
-
-	dev->mt76.vif_mask = 0;
-	dev->mt76.beacon_mask = 0;
 }
 
 /* Only after the frames left in the hardware queues have been completed:
@@ -616,6 +626,8 @@ static void mt76x02_watchdog_reset(struc
 	mt76_clear(dev, MT_WPDMA_GLO_CFG,
 		   MT_WPDMA_GLO_CFG_TX_DMA_EN | MT_WPDMA_GLO_CFG_RX_DMA_EN);
 	usleep_range(5000, 10000);
+	if (restart)
+		mt76x02_sync_tx_pn(dev);
 	mt76_wr(dev, MT_INT_SOURCE_CSR, 0xffffffff);
 
 	/* let fw reset DMA */
